{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat upon the blood.</b> Without slaughter. And thus it says: ״ושחטתם בזה ואכלתם״ etc., ״ולא תחטאו לה׳ לאכול על הדם.״ Another interpretation: <b>You shall not eat upon the blood, you shall not divine.</b> You who are redeemers of the blood — you shall not divine by eating upon the blood. The meaning: upon the grave of the slain man, in order to protect yourselves from being avenged, for this is the custom of the Amorites. And because it mentioned ״לא תאכלו על הדם״ which is a custom of the Amorites, it mentioned after it the rest of their customs."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The second interpretation reads ואכלתם in the prooftext as ואכלתם, resolving it mechanically as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:38.046213170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}